stead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"source\":\"campaign-creatives\",\"language\":\"English\",\"lastError\":null,\"imageModel\":\"openai/gpt-image-2:100\",\"hasNSFWRisk\":false,\"imagePrompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Grounded in the FAB (Features, Advantages, Benefits) framework, this minimalist studio-product ad is designed for top-of-funnel discovery to capture users looking to upgrade their beauty routine. The visual hero is the physical transformation of the product: a high-resolution, macro action shot of a clean, hand-held gold spoon dropping the fine powder into a pristine glass of water, showing it dissolve into a beautiful, swirling, translucent golden-orange liquid, with the sleek matte white Wellbeing Nutrition jar standing clean in the background. The design uses a warm Wellness Cream background (#fff9eb) with a light grid overlay at 0.1 opacity to suggest scientific precision. The minimal headline, \\\"Upgrade your daily skin collagen,\\\" is positioned in clean, modern Outfit typography across the top, keeping the total text space under 15%. T