\\\"), accented by a bolded \\\"Type I & III\\\" label and a distinct white horizontal banner displaying \\\"Valencia Orange Flavour\\\" (or \\\"Piña Colada Flavor\\\" on the older variant). To the right of this central box sits a circular gold emblem displaying a white, multi-faceted geometric sphere grid, bordered on the right by the curved black text \\\"Wild Caught • Mercury Free\\\", positioned below a small gold \\\"Clinically Approved\\\" cross badge and adjacent to bold black text reading \\\"8g Collagen per serving\\\". The bottom margin of the label features five simple black line-art icons representing \\\"Brightening\\\", \\\"Hydration\\\", \\\"Elasticity\\\", \\\"Anti-ageing\\\", and \\\"Protection\\\", flanked by weight specifications of \\\"Net Wt.: 250 g\\\" on the left and classification text on the right. When the fine, light-colored inner powder is mixed with water, it dissolves into a translucent, vibrant golden-orange liquid.\\n\\nUse the product appearance text only as a private visual reference for accurately drawing the product. Do not print, quote, paraphrase, label, or turn any of that description into ad copy. Treat orientation-specific details carefully: show front-only details only when the product front is visible; if the brief shows the back, side, top, or an angled view where those details would not be visible, omit them instead of moving them onto the wrong face.\\n\\nThe attached product photos show the real product — reproduce it faithfully.\\n\\nDesign requirements (apply to this ad):\\n- Follow the instructions by the director.\\n- Make the ad design, layout, typography on-branded, but should look premium, editorial-like.\\n- Establish a clear visual hierarchy: one dominant focal point the eye lands on\\n  first, then the supporting message, then the CTA.\\n- Keep strong figure/ground contrast. If text sits over imagery, place a scrim or\\n  overlay behind it so it stays fully legible.\\n- Place the focal subject on a rule-of-thirds line; leave generous whitespace and\\n  avoid clutter.\\n- Use a limited palette anchored to the brand colors (~60-30-10), reserving one\\n  accent color for the call to action.\\n- Keep 20% space all around the creative for the ad to look cleaner\\n- Group and align elements cleanly (Gestalt); use at most two type styles.\",\"source\":\"campaign-creatives\",\"language\":\"English\",\"lastError\":null,\"imageModel\":\"openai/gpt-image-2:100\",\"hasNSFWRisk\":false,\"imagePrompt\":\"Instructions by the director: Using the PAS (Problem-Agitate-Solve) framework, this bold split-graphic 1:1 ad acts as a high-contrast pattern interrupt to hook people experiencing dull skin barrier issues. The visual hero is the stark contrast between a black-and-white flat-lay image of a cluttered vanity showing tired, dry skincare routines, and a vibrant, color-burst circular cutout in the center revealing the bright golden-orange collagen liquid being stirred. The headline, \\\"Tired of dull morning skin?\\\", is rendered in bold black Circular Std at the top, taking up less than 10% of the overall layout to respect the text limits. A subtle image of the Wellbeing Nutrition jar sits tucked in the bottom corner of the colorful circle to introduce the solution naturally. The single call to action is a sharp-edged, flat-rectangular orange button in primary brand orange (#ff5000) that reads \\\"see how it works.\\\" Brand alignment instructions: Rely on high contrast between the muted mist-gray background (#f2f4f7) and the energetic brand orange (#ff5000); keep the copy minimal and leverage the stark, graphic split to emphasize the immediate shift from dullness to skin hydration.\\n\\nProduct appearance: This product is a dietary supplement packaged in a wide, cylindrical, matte white opaque plastic jar with a matching flat-topped, screw-on white cap featuring rounded upper edges. The jar features a wrap-around label with a smooth vertical color gradient transitioning from clean white 